core=dict(status='usable',rationale='Both core lines have been followed through actual dispatch, producers, quorum consumers, context changes, configuration activation and caller handoffs. Usable is a bounded source explanation, not safety proof or execution evidence.',core_gaps=[],open_details=['Exact storage failure recovery for a production backend lies beyond the library snapshot; MemoryStorage is not a durable backend.','Detailed read-release liveness under configuration-triggered commitment remains a local question.','Progress flow-control variants and malformed input behavior require separate bounded questions.'])
core['formation']=dict(explanation='A caller proposes through RawNode or Node.run. Followers may forward; leaders reject proposals during transfer/removal or quota exhaustion. Accepted entries get leader term and consecutive index, enter unstable log and generate deferred self append support. Replication carries preceding index/term, entries and commit. Followers match the preceding entry, refuse committed conflicts, append only the conflicting suffix and acknowledge through the resulting prefix; stale prefixes can acknowledge the existing committed boundary. Ready or asynchronous local append envelopes impose the storage-before-response contract. Successful current-term tracked replies update per-peer Match. The active voter majority order statistic, minimum across both joint halves, supplies a candidate commit index; raftLog advances only when its entry term matches current leader term. Append broadcasts and bounded heartbeat commit propagate the decision. Ready then supplies committed entries, with asynchronous application restricted to locally stable entries and snapshots blocking entry application. Advance or apply response reports completion; the caller owns actual state-machine effects and client acknowledgement. Propose success alone is not commitment.',behavior_ids=['B-entry','B-propose','B-follower-append','B-storage-release','B-aggregate','B-apply'],fact_ids=['F-app-queued','F-match','F-committed','F-apply-reported'],source_ids=['entry','leader-admit','candidate-follower','send-replication','append-receive','log-start-append','reply-queue','async-contract','leader-match','tracker-commit','majority','joint','log-eligibility','log-apply','ready-contract','node-loop'])
core['context']=dict(explanation='Election ticks or Campaign pass eligibility and unapplied-configuration guards. PreVote collects support without changing term/vote; real campaign increments term and records self vote, counted only after deferred response release. Incoming votes require voting eligibility and last term/index freshness. The candidate accepts its phase-specific response type, records first vote per identity and uses active joint voter quorums; winning installs leadership and an empty entry. Higher term normally resets role, votes, remote progress and readOnly acknowledgements, with pre-vote and check-quorum lease exceptions. Lower-term replies do not reach ordinary consumers. Same-term leader traffic demotes candidates. Optional CheckQuorum revokes local leadership on inactive quorum; transfer catches up a voter then sends TimeoutNow, rejects new proposals while pending and aborts on timeout. Application activates membership; learner promotion/removal and joint exit change future quorum interpretation. Restart loads term/vote/commit and membership from Storage then becomes follower. Snapshot restore preserves committed prefix constraints, replaces history/config if needed and prevents campaigning while installation is pending.',behavior_ids=['B-campaign','B-election-result','B-context','B-membership','B-recovery'],fact_ids=['F-vote-queued','F-leader','F-config','F-committed'],source_ids=['campaign','step-vote','roles','term-filter','ticks','candidate-follower','leader-other','tracker-votes','majority','joint','config-change','config-activate','startup','snapshot-restore'])
core['connection']=dict(explanation='Formation support is scoped by current role/term and interpreted by application-activated membership. Reset discards remote Match and prior vote/read acknowledgements but does not erase log or committed prefix; election freshness and current-term commit gating reconnect inherited history to new decisions. Configuration changes preserve existing peer Match, initialize new peers at zero, and recompute commitment under new voters; staged learners remain outgoing voters until joint exit. Queued storage completions keep their originating raft term: stale entry append completion cannot trim unstable entries, while committed snapshot/application completion remains meaningful across terms. Pending pre-current-term ReadIndex requests survive reset separately from the cleared heartbeat acknowledgement tracker; a subsequent current-term commit reprocesses them through current read mode/quorum. Ready read results still require caller correlation and application progress. Storage, configuration and application boundaries therefore directly govern A1 support and A2 eligibility, without treating mere message emission or applied bookkeeping as durable or client completion.',behavior_ids=['B-context','B-storage-release','B-membership','B-aggregate','B-read','B-apply','B-recovery'],fact_ids=['F-match','F-committed','F-config','F-read-index','F-apply-reported'],source_ids=['reset-append','log-eligibility','config-change','config-activate','term-filter','storage-envelope','storage-tail','unstable-stable','apply-progress','read-pending','read-tracking','ready-contract'])
